# Real manager continuation: baseline before new capabilities

The operator permits starting local WSL and exactly owned temporary diagnostic
service/slice. Existing services, clocks, production keys, release installation,
worker execution and the dedicated server remain outside this scope. Earlier
temporary diagnostic bootstrap/account/enrollment permission is retained; all
absence, inode/hash and cleanup guards are unchanged from the existing fixture.

The sole shell change is a new exclusive lane whitelist. Old consumed lanes are
not rerun. The exact previously passing original zbus 6 graph is reused, under
its frozen source receipt and unchanged protected root inputs. A fresh release
libtest/bootstrap build avoids changing any original execution window. Commands
remain offline/locked, 1200 outer/1100 inner, 4 GiB floors, five-second retirement;
the actual readiness fixture retains its old 120-second fail-safe and 300/60/10
origins. Native source and artifacts are checked before dispatch.

The baseline dispatches exactly the existing one-shot original-manager readiness
case and records its first outcome. Its cleanup-before-EOF ordering is explicitly
NOT autonomous all-writer proof, worker release, completion or reconnect. First
establish real delivery; then strengthen cessation before cleanup and join actual
generation-bound observation/reconnect, preserving the baseline and all guards.

New native execution is single-use, not automatic retry-to-pass. All stdout/stderr
files exist before preflight. No helper can promote absent send/readiness, empty
selection or successful cleanup to a passed original-delivery result.
